      "content": "the voices are a good start but i think they're a bit too \"extreme\" in their slang. for the new residents, maybe make them sound a bit more \"polished\" or educated? like, they're the ones with the degrees and the corporate jobs moving in. and for the locals, can you lean more into the grit? maybe add some more aggressive or \"street\" elements to their speech to really show that they're the ones who might get pushed around or act out because they're losing their territory? i want that contrast between the \"civilized\" newcomers and the more \"raw\" locals to really pop.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
